#!/usr/bin/env bash
#
# exbloattv: debloat an Android TV / Google TV box from a Mac or Linux computer, over ADB.
#
# The same flow as the ExBloat TV phone app, in a terminal:
#   find the TV -> turn on debugging -> read its apps -> keep what you watch -> review -> clean up -> undo any time.
#
# It shares the app's record of changes and run lock on the TV (/data/local/tmp/exbloattv/state.json): the app's
# "Undo everything" reverses what this script did, `exbloattv undo` reverses what the app did, and the two never
# clean the same TV at the same time.
#
# Needs bash 3.2 or later (macOS's /bin/bash is fine), adb, curl (only to download the new home screen) and the
# usual POSIX tools. Nothing else. MIT licence. https://github.com/XploreDatum/exbloattv
#
# Layout: constants, generated catalog + safety lists, output, small helpers, adb, JSON, the TV's state file,
# finding and connecting, reading the TV, choosing, planning, running, home screen swap, restart, undo, commands.

